# Amazing-Hand-Project

A structured robotics documentation and system model for the **AmazingHand servo-actuated robotic hand system**.  That I have been assigned by the company that I am currently an intern at ZeroBionic Africa.
This repository breaks down the hardware, software, control flow, calibration, and finger-level kinematics into a clear engineering model.

---

##  Project Purpose

The goal of this project is to:

- Understand the architecture of a servo-actuated robotic hand
- Model how software controls physical finger movement
- Document calibration and servo mapping systems
- Provide a contributor-friendly robotics system breakdown
- Serve as a foundation for further robotics development and research

---

## System Overview

The AmazingHand system is composed of:

- Servo-driven actuators
- 3D-printed finger segments
- servo-based transmission system
- Microcontroller-based firmware (Arduino/STM32 class)
- Python-based control interface
- Serial communication pipeline

---

## System Architecture
```bash
User Input
↓
Command Interface (GUI / Script / API)
↓
Python Control Layer
↓
Serial Communication
↓
Microcontroller Firmware
↓
PWM Signal Generation
↓
Servo Actuation
↓
servo Mechanics
↓
Finger Movement

```
